<section class="section section--flush page-hero"><div class="container prose"><h1>HomeMaster</h1></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Modular smart home automation with local logic</h2><figure><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/product-lineup.png" alt="HomeMaster retail boxes for OpenTherm Gateway, Digital I/O, Analog I/O, Water Leak, MicroPLC and Energy Meter modules" width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster retail boxes for OpenTherm Gateway, Digital I/O, Analog I/O, Water Leak, MicroPLC and Energy Meter modules</figcaption></figure>
<p><strong>HomeMaster</strong> is the in-house brand of ISYSTEMS AUTOMATION: DIN-rail modules and controllers for lighting, heating, energy metering, leak detection and boiler control — with logic on every module, RS-485 Modbus between devices, and integration through ESPHome and Home Assistant. No cloud dependency; the system keeps working when the network does not.</p>
<p>The product range, shop, system configurator and documentation live at <a href="https://www.home-master.eu">home-master.eu</a>.</p></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><div class="grid grid--2 point-grid">
<div><h2 class="section-title">Deterministic communication</h2><p>RS-485 Modbus RTU between modules — stable on long cable runs and in electrically noisy panels.</p></div>
<div><h3>Modular and scalable</h3><p>DIN-rail I/O, metering, dimming, leak detection and alarm modules expand around a MiniPLC or MicroPLC controller as the installation grows.</p></div>
<div><h3>Local logic on every module</h3><p>Wall-switch scenes, shutter interlocks, valve shut-off, load balancing and boiler interfaces can run on the module itself. Critical functions continue if the controller or Wi-Fi link is down.</p></div>
<div><h3>Fully local operation</h3><p>Automation runs on the devices in the panel. Internet is optional — for remote access and updates, not for day-to-day control.</p></div>
</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Controllers</h2><h2 class="section-title">MiniPLC</h2><div class="section-promo__layout section-promo__layout--card"><figure class="figure--embed"><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/miniplc-product.jpg" alt="HomeMaster MiniPLC DIN-rail controller with display, relays and RS-485" width="960" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster MiniPLC DIN-rail controller with display, relays and RS-485</figcaption></figure><div class="section-promo__text"><p>DIN-rail controller with relays, I/O, temperature inputs, display and integrated supply. RS-485 Modbus expansion for a full cabinet from one unit.</p></div></div>
<h2 class="section-title">MicroPLC</h2><div class="section-promo__layout section-promo__layout--card"><figure class="figure--embed"><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/microplc-product.jpg" alt="HomeMaster MicroPLC ESP32 DIN-rail controller" width="960" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster MicroPLC ESP32 DIN-rail controller</figcaption></figure><div class="section-promo__text"><p>Compact ESP32 controller for smaller panels: one relay, digital input, RS-485 and Wi-Fi. Controls the Modbus module bus without the cost of a full PLC when the I/O lives on the modules.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">DIN-rail modules</h2><ul>
<li><strong>DIO-430-R1</strong> — relay and digital input module; wall switches, scenes and shutter interlock handled locally.</li>
<li><strong>AIO-422-R1</strong> — 0–10 V in and out, PT100/PT1000 RTD on one module.</li>
<li><strong>ENM-223-R1</strong> — three-phase energy metering, power quality events and load balancing.</li>
<li><strong>WLD-521-R1</strong> — five leak zones, valve shut-off and water metering.</li>
<li><strong>OTGW-R1</strong> — OpenTherm boiler interface; ESPHome-native.</li>
<li><strong>DIM-420-R1</strong> — AC dimmer for lighting circuits.</li>
<li><strong>RGB-621-R1</strong> — RGBCCT LED control.</li>
<li><strong>STR-3221-R1</strong> — stair and corridor LED sequencing.</li>
<li><strong>ALM-173-R1</strong> — alarm and security inputs.</li>
</ul>
