</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">In the panel</h2><figure><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/din-rail-modules-row.jpg" alt="HomeMaster DIN-rail modules and MiniPLC controller mounted on a galvanized backplate" width="1280" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster DIN-rail modules and MiniPLC controller mounted on a galvanized backplate</figcaption></figure>
<p>Modules share a 35 mm DIN rail, terminal blocks and RS-485 bus — the same layout whether the panel serves one apartment or a small building.</p>
<figure><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/control-panel-wired.jpg" alt="Wired HomeMaster control panel with MiniPLC, I/O modules and circuit protection" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>Wired HomeMaster control panel with MiniPLC, I/O modules and circuit protection</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Designed and built in-house</h2><figure><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/miniplc-pcb-top.jpg" alt="HomeMaster MiniPLC printed circuit board with ESP32, display header and field terminals" width="1280" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster MiniPLC printed circuit board with ESP32, display header and field terminals</figcaption></figure>
<p>Every HomeMaster product is designed, assembled and tested at our premises in Ploiești. Firmware, schematics and ESPHome packages are published open source on GitHub.</p>
<div class="gallery">
<figure><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/pcb-assembly-stages.jpg" alt="HomeMaster printed circuit boards at bare-board and populated assembly stages" width="1280" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster printed circuit boards at bare-board and populated assembly stages</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src="/assets/img/homemaster/bench-test-rig.jpg" alt="HomeMaster modules on a bench test rig with automated test equipment" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>HomeMaster modules on a bench test rig with automated test equipment</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<p>Eleven modules have been taken through EU conformity assessment for EMC, LVD, RED and RoHS, with Declarations of Conformity issued for each. The electrical-safety and EMC test capability built for that work is described under <a href="/compliance.html">Compliance and Testing</a>.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Open source and documentation</h2><p>Hardware, firmware and ESPHome YAML for every module are on GitHub. Modbus register maps, integration examples for Home Assistant and application notes are on <a href="https://www.home-master.eu">home-master.eu</a>.</p>
<p>The online configurator lists the exact modules, enclosure size and DIN-rail layout for a described installation, with live shop prices — see <a href="https://www.home-master.eu">Build your system</a> on the brand site.</p></div></section>
